        "**Moderate (grade 3) infection needs a broader, often initially parenteral, regimen covering Gram-positive cocci, Gram-negative bacilli and anaerobes for 1-3 weeks** - amoxicillin-clavulanate or ampicillin-sulbactam, or a cephalosporin plus metronidazole, or piperacillin-tazobactam - and de-escalation to a culture-guided oral agent as soon as the patient improves.",
