        "**Footwear advice is specific in the Indian setting:** avoid open chappals, thong sandals with a toe post and hard-soled slippers; use **closed, broad, deep-toed footwear with a cushioned microcellular rubber (MCR) sole, fitted in the evening when the foot is largest**, worn with seamless cotton socks, and broken in gradually over a few hours a day; **custom insoles or moulded footwear are prescribed for a deformed foot or after a healed ulcer.**",
